("h2", "3.9. Training as one virtual computer"),
("p", "With GB300, the {it_mw} MW correspond to {tr_secadores_net_normal_gb300_nvl72_gpus} GPUs ({tr_secadores_net_normal_gb300_nvl72_ef} EF peak FP8). Synchronising every 100 steps keeps communication overhead at {tr_secadores_net_normal_gb300_nvl72_ov100}%, so the whole network has theoretical capacity for 10²⁷ FLOP in {tr_secadores_net_normal_gb300_nvl72_m6} months from a June start, against {tr_quantum_200mw_gb300_nvl72_m6} months for Quantum, and each regional cluster for a 3×10²⁶-FLOP model in 1–2 months (Table §T:training§, Fig. §F:training§; Supplementary notes). Synchronous training over Spectrum-XGS gives the same time if each span carries {xs_gb_pairs} fibre pairs instead of {xs_pairs_base} (US${xs_gb_capex} million more in optics); with {xs_pairs_base} pairs overhead would be {xs_gb_ov_xgs}%."),
